        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Crimson silk length, Agra, ca. 1855."@en , "Lengths of silk such as this were categorised as 'piece goods', fabrics made to standard dimensions for sale. Piece goods could be used for a variety of purposes. Silk such as this length was often used to make or line garments."@en , "Length of crimson silk with narrow yellow borders, cut"@en ;
